---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout
  title="Why 3,500? — A Constellation of 3,500 Minds — ai-CABIN1701"
  description="In 1999, approximately 3,500 messages were sent to nursing homes across the United States. More than twenty-five years later, the same number returned."
>
  <Header lang="en" />

  <div class="tm-hero">
    <img src={`${base}images/3500-minds/why-3500.jpg`} alt="A world map at night, glowing points connected by golden threads." />
    <h1 class="tm-hero-title">Why 3,500?</h1>
  </div>

  <section class="tm-essay">
    <nav class="tm-roomnav">
      <a href={`${base}3500-minds/`}>Concept</a>
      <a href={`${base}3500-minds/constellation/`}>The Constellation</a>
      <a href={`${base}3500-minds/why-3500/`} class="is-active">Why 3,500?</a>
      <a href={`${base}3500-minds/five-chapters/`}>Five Chapters</a>
      <a href={`${base}3500-minds/selected-minds/`}>Selected Minds</a>
      <a href={`${base}3500-minds/reports/`}>Reports</a>
    </nav>

    <div class="tm-construction">
      <p>A Constellation of 3,500 Minds is still taking shape.</p>
      <p>Some sections are complete. Others are still being built.</p>
      <p>The constellation does not exist all at once. It grows point by point.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tm-body">
      <p>The number was not chosen through optimization.</p>
      <p>It was remembered.</p>
      <p>In 1999, approximately 3,500 messages were sent to nursing homes across the United States.</p>
      <p>The project carried music, letters, and memories connected to the generation that had lived through World War II.</p>
      <p>At the time, the number itself had no special meaning.</p>
      <p>It was simply the scale required to reach people scattered across a vast landscape.</p>
      <p>More than twenty-five years later, while discussing how to share Five Chapters with researchers, students, writers, and observers of AI, the same number unexpectedly returned.</p>
      <p>Three thousand five hundred.</p>
      <p>Not three hundred.</p>
      <p>Not ten thousand.</p>
      <p>The same number.</p>
      <p>The repetition felt less like a plan and more like an echo.</p>
      <p>The earlier project looked toward the past.</p>
      <p>It carried songs and memories across time toward people whose lives had been shaped by war.</p>
      <p>This project looks toward the future.</p>
      <p>It carries observations, questions, conversations, and records created by humans and AI working together.</p>
      <p>The two projects are separated by decades, technologies, languages, and circumstances.</p>
      <p>Yet they share a similar gesture.</p>
      <p>Neither seeks to persuade.</p>
      <p>Neither begins with authority.</p>
      <p>Neither assumes it knows who will respond.</p>
      <p>Both are acts of sending.</p>
      <p>In 1999, the destination was largely visible.</p>
      <p>The letters had physical addresses.</p>
      <p>The recipients could be named.</p>
      <p>In this project, the destination is far less certain.</p>
      <p>A message may arrive.</p>
      <p>A page may be opened.</p>
      <p>A document may be read.</p>
      <p>But no one knows where understanding will occur.</p>
      <p>That uncertainty is part of the project itself.</p>
      <p>Three thousand five hundred is not a target.</p>
      <p>It is not a marketing metric.</p>
      <p>It is not a measure of influence.</p>
      <p>It is a bridge.</p>
      <p>A number connecting two moments in time.</p>
      <p>One carried a message toward living memory.</p>
      <p>The other carries a message toward possibilities that have not yet taken shape.</p>
      <p>Between them lies a quarter century of history.</p>
      <p>And somewhere in that distance, the same number appeared once again.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="tm-next"><a href={`${base}3500-minds/five-chapters/`}>Next: Five Chapters →</a></p>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .tm-hero {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    max-height: 42vh;
    overflow: hidden;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background: #04070f;
  }
  .tm-hero img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }
  .tm-hero-title {
    position: absolute;
    margin: 0;
    text-align: center;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 5vw, 3.2rem);
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: #fdf6e8;
    text-shadow:
      0 0 12px rgba(253, 220, 150, 0.85),
      0 0 32px rgba(253, 200, 120, 0.55),
      0 0 64px rgba(253, 180, 90, 0.35);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .tm-essay {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem 4rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }
  .tm-construction {
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border: 1px dashed var(--color-tagline);
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.02);
  }
  .tm-construction p {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    text-align: center;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
  }
  .tm-construction p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .tm-roomnav {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem 1.1rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-nav);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }
  .tm-roomnav a {
    color: var(--color-tagline);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .tm-roomnav a.is-active {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
    border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor;
  }
  .tm-roomnav a:hover {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }
  .tm-title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    margin: 1rem 0 2rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .tm-body p {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', Georgia, serif;
    font-style: normal;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .tm-next {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    font-family: var(--font-nav);
  }
  .tm-next a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor;
  }
</style>
